-- title:
--   Uniformiser germ and stalk dimension at the generic point of C₁
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$ and $M\neq 0$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $C_1,C_2$ be $k$-schemes, each proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, together with closed immersions $i_1,i_2$ of $C_1,C_2$ into the base change $X_k=\operatorname{pullback}$ of the structure morphism [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A (↥K) j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) along $\operatorname{Spec} k\to\operatorname{Spec} A$, commuting with the structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} k$. Assume every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced with finite cardinality $n>0$, there is a section $\varepsilon$ of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A (↥K) j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and sections $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ of $C_1,C_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equal to the base change `sectionBaseChange k ε` of $\varepsilon$, and finally that there exists $w$ consisting of a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion whose reduction `intSeriesC k` is nonzero. The conclusion: for every $\varpi\in A$ generating the maximal ideal of $A$ and every $\xi\in C_1$ whose closure is all of $C_1$, writing $z$ for the image of $\xi$ under $i_1$ followed by the first projection $X_k\to X$, where $X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout of the two affine charts, the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ through the structure morphism [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and $\dim \mathcal O_{X,z}\le 1$.
--
--   The two assertions are precisely the hypotheses — that $z$ lies on the special fibre, and that the local ring there has Krull dimension at most one — under which the stalk of the two-chart integral model at $z$ is a valuation ring of $K$ lying over $A$. The statement is used in the identification of that stalk, for the first of the two components of the geometric special fibre of the model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$.
